# RSM option resumption: bounded prospective curriculum

2026-10-10 UTC; actual author `/root/research_architect`. Read with NEW `schemas/RSM_OPTION_RESUMPTION_V1.md` and its prospective configuration. This is design readiness only: no interpreter, generation, gold, scoring, model run or approval. Legacy RSM-001 and all accepted releases remain frozen.

## Actual measured gap and source boundary

Root's completed `research/research_gap_analysis/RSM_NEXT_GAP_MEASURE.json` SHA256 `99f8348b350e48410f35ab99d87a9c3cb7a0fbb5ff1f383e7c3f92bac2d074af` measures the actual RSM v0001 input grammar: 24 accepted records from 12 source families, 20 train/4 exposed-development rows and 10/2 families. All 12 already contain nested calls of maximum depth 2–3, condition depth 1 and two integer registers, using add/scale/swap/call/if. Arguments, initiation/success contracts and interruption/checkpoint/resume are absent from that grammar. Thus adding call depth alone would not close this gap. This author read its completed report and freeze, the existing public curriculum/semantics, and one approved input, while verifying the complete approved file hash; no new producer implementation or targets were inspected. The reported counts are root's static measurements, not a fresh measurement or learner result by this author.

The local proposed research card `rineya_complementary_research_2026-10-09/02_research_tracks/RSM-001.md` asks for initiation, bindings, termination and interruption/recovery, and distinguishes an executed supplied procedure from learned internalization. Its local resource inventory anchors P07/P08/P09/P34 are motivation only here; this task does not implement expert iteration, DAgger, option discovery or the proposed experiment arms. All exact local evidence paths/hashes are recorded in the design execution receipt.

| Measured missing grammar | New bounded mechanism and decisive evidence |
|---|---|
| Formal arguments/local bindings absent | Entry-time integer arguments copied into immutable frames; live registers later change; a saved argument must affect a later primitive/guard/exit. Positive argument counterfactual remains feasible and changes trace/outcome. |
| Initiation absent | Check an explicit multi-atom entry predicate before effects; matched one-argument pass/fail control. Resume keeps a previously entered option even if the current state would fail its entry predicate. |
| Success/termination contract absent | Check the supplied postcondition on exhausted-body return; matched success predicate changes success versus failure without changing executed effects. No rollback or early termination is inferred. |
| Interruptions and resume absent | Exact committed event prefix plus canonical active frames; continue pending work, retaining selected branch and advanced caller cursor. Compare to uninterrupted suffix. |
| Duplicate non-idempotent effects cannot be supervised explicitly | Visible restart versus resume of the same valid checkpoint; completed nonzero add/active scale/swap effects must produce a measured continuation/state/status difference when replayed. |
| Repeated interruption absent | Second actual checkpoint, short event-budget pause and subsequent suffix control; prove the remaining work rather than counting interruption labels. |

These are coverage hypotheses. No learning benefit, retention result or unaided composition success is established.

## Small initial cohort and independence

Plan **12 fresh source-program families**, organized in four mechanism strata with three genuinely different source graphs per stratum. Use family indices `{12,13,18}`, `{14,15,19}`, `{16,17,28}`, `{20,21,29}`: each stratum has two train families and one exposed-development family under the existing index%10 policy. Indices18,19,28,29 are dev; the other eight are train. Reserved holes are not dataset families. Do not reuse accepted RSM lineages0..11 as new sources.

Strata emphasize (1) saved entry arguments consumed after state mutation, (2) nested child return and advanced caller continuation, (3) retained selected branch with a later guard reversal, and (4) ordered noncommuting reusable calls plus entry/exit obligations. Every family still supplies the common controls below. The strata are four broad mechanism classes, not 12 mechanisms or a claim of held-out mechanism learning. Require all 12 normalized call/branch/read-write dependency graphs to differ beyond option/register/parameter names, constants, styling and cut locations. A renamed program, checkpoint, argument value, view or reordered object is a correlated descendant. If a proposed family is isomorphic, replace it before generation rather than counting it as fresh.

Every family has nine matched semantic contexts and two object-field styles: **108 tasks / 216 correlated rendered records**, 144 train/72 exposed-dev. Contexts do not add independent families. The complete program graph and all descendants stay within one split. Report actual call-graph, control-flow and def-use signatures against legacy inputs and across the pilot. These splits expose all four mechanism strata on dev; they do not seal OOD or hide the contract, and may share primitive motifs. Future novel-composition claims need a separately frozen template holdout experiment.

| Context | Actual task/control obligation |
|---|---|
| F | Fresh complete successful execution with ample event budget. Root guard and exit are true; binds and consumes an argument; two option levels and at least one real state-dependent branch. |
| R | Resume at first true checkpoint inside an active nested option, after a committed effect and before meaningful future work; complete with F's exact suffix/terminal state/status. At least one caller cursor, saved binding and selected branch are retained. |
| T | Change only R.mode to restart. Root initiation must pass and at least one committed non-idempotent effect must actually execute again; actual trace plus terminal state/status differs from R. Identify the repeated effect and its exact second effect on state. A blocked root entry cannot substitute for this replay witness; I separately covers entry failure. |
| P | Change only R.event_budget to a positive shorter budget. Must pause at a distinct, later, still-running checkpoint with at least one new effect committed and pending future effect/return work. No metadata-only interruption claim. |
| U | Resume from the true second checkpoint reached by P; history is the original F prefix extended by P.new_events. Complete with F's exact remaining suffix, preserving argument/branch/caller custody across both cuts. |
| A | Change one root argument expression in F; both initiate and complete successfully. Actual argument-dependent primitive/branch or final state differs. Maintain every other program/entry field and initial state. |
| I | Change one root argument expression in F so root initiation is false. No body effect executes. A single public predicate atom must decisively change; all other root initiation atoms remain true. |
| S | Change one constant expression in one atom of the root success predicate from F. Entry/body behavior and all effect events are identical; root return changes successful to success_failed. All other root success atoms remain true. This is a contract revision sibling, not an arbitrary wrong target. |
| X | Change exactly one consequential field in R.checkpoint while keeping its history unchanged. Cycle state/cursor/binding tampering across families; output is invalid_checkpoint and no new effect. Mutated field must be active, not an unused binding or an exhausted irrelevant branch. |

The first cut must have committed a real effect, at least two active option frames plus a selected branch frame, and a saved argument that is subsequently consumed. The R checkpoint's current state must make one already entered **non-root** option's initiation false, while its originally checked entry was true; resuming must still be valid. Root initiation must remain true when T restarts from that same state. This separates retaining a valid active child from replaying completed root/child effects. P must make an additional effect and leave work for U. These requirements are simultaneous, not nine independent annotations. An independent public-only oracle must first establish that small handmade programs can satisfy them; if not, publish a new prospective revision before producing any candidate, rather than weaken a gate silently. No literal candidate, cut, frame or target is specified here.

## Bounds, difficulty and independent verification

Selected limits: 2–4 options, 1–3 parameters per option, maximum simultaneous option depth 3, syntactic conditional depth 2, at most24 declared instructions counting both branches, and at most48 complete semantic events. Initial integers are -6..6 and prospective valid-run intermediate registers stay in -4096..4096; semantic arithmetic itself remains exact/unbounded. Bound arguments/constants so the actual complete traces satisfy those limits. F/R/U/A full budgets are48; P has a measured shorter positive budget. Every valid fresh body contains at least three actual effects and a parameter-dependent effect; neither a long unused branch nor a supplied history inflates difficulty.

Label difficulty from actual dependencies: Level2 component controls cover one guard, one binding or one invalid checkpoint. Level3 family instances require the nested caller, selected branch and saved-value dependence together. Level4 is allowed only if the answer additionally requires at least two dependent option completions/noncommuting effects across the interruption; report the decisive intermediate states. Do not award Levels5–7 from nesting, row count or two style views. Next_event at a pause is a deterministic execution query, not learned action selection or optimal planning.

Before production, an independently authored exact interpreter and separate primitive/event simulator must agree on handmade boundary cases, all legal event cuts, all budgets through completion, argument snapshotting, branch retention, empty bodies/branches, failed entry/exit, root/child returns, boolean-as-integer malformed values and history/stack mismatches. Confirm the schema's finite unique result; object key order cannot change it. No shortest-path or arbitrary tie-breaking teacher is needed because the supplied policy fixes every transition.

For future candidate audits publish exact source/spec/candidate/manifest hashes and real execution receipts; per-family/context/split status/effect/horizon/frame-depth/argument-use histograms; every actual matched diff, frame snapshot, suffix and replay trap; normalized structural novelty; field-pair equality; false-code exclusion and first-failure custody. Match controls using actual records and complete typed inputs, not context letters or claimed counts. Negative X status and restart status may be correlated with visible requests by design: measure the majority/simple mode/history-length baselines and do not describe this as shortcut-free. With only12 source families, table/program memorization remains plausible. Longer recovery, recursion, noisy/stale external histories, unknown effects, asynchronous concurrency and generalized retry policies are out of scope.

Later producer/oracle/expert/red/adjudicator executions are separate. Fresh prediction-before-gold review and actual adjudication are required for approval. This author designed prior factory curricula and may later adjudicate this design but has generated no future sample and provides no verdict here. Root supplied the measured gaps; shared-model/common-guidance errors and later design/adjudication overlap must be disclosed. All new design files are local after the current checkpoint inventory until a later verified backup.
